const e={id:"int-cors-and-proxy",title:{en:"CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:9,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. What is CORS & Why Does Every MERN Beginner Encounter It?",hi:"1. CORS Kya Hai Aur Har MERN Developer Ko Yeh Error Kyun Milta Hai?"},body:{en:`Almost every web developer building their first MERN application experiences this dreaded red error in the browser console:

> \`Access to XMLHttpRequest at 'http://localhost:5000/api/users' from origin 'http://localhost:5173' has been blocked by CORS policy: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.\`

### What is the Same-Origin Policy (SOP)?
Web browsers enforce a strict security mechanism called the **Same-Origin Policy**. By default, JavaScript running in a browser page is only allowed to make HTTP requests to the **exact same origin** that served the page.

An **Origin** is defined by three components:
\`\`\`text
Protocol  +  Domain (Host)  +  Port
https://     +  example.com    +  :443
\`\`\`
If ANY of these three differs, the browser considers it a **Cross-Origin** request:
- \`http://localhost:5173\` (React Vite dev server)
- \`http://localhost:5000\` (Express API server)
Even though both are running on your laptop's \`localhost\`, their **ports are different (5173 vs 5000)**! Therefore, your browser blocks the frontend from reading the backend's response unless explicitly allowed by CORS.

### What is CORS?
**Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)** is an HTTP-header based protocol that allows a server to tell the browser: *"Yes, I recognize requests coming from origin http://localhost:5173, and I give the browser permission to read my response."*`,hi:`Jab koi bhi developer pehli baar React ko Express se connect karta hai, toh browser console mein yeh red error zaroor aata hai:
> \`blocked by CORS policy: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present...\`

### Same-Origin Policy (SOP) Kya Hai?
Browser ke andar ek strict security guard hota hai jise **Same-Origin Policy** kehte hain. Yeh guard bolta hai ki koi bhi website sirf apne hi origin par data bhej sakti hai ya receive kar sakti hai.

**Origin** teen cheezon se milkar banta hai:
\`Protocol\` + \`Domain\` + \`Port\`

MERN local development mein:
- React chal raha hai: \`http://localhost:5173\`
- Express chal raha hai: \`http://localhost:5000\`
Dono ka port alag hai (5173 vs 5000)! Isliye browser ise alag origin manta hai aur response ko block kar deta hai.

### CORS Kya Hai?
**CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)** HTTP headers ka ek standard hai jisme Express server browser ko batata hai: *"Haan, http://localhost:5173 meri apni frontend app hai, iska data block mat karo!"*`}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"2. The Preflight Request (HTTP OPTIONS Method)",hi:"2. Preflight Request: Browser Pehle OPTIONS Call Kyun Bhejta Hai?"},body:{en:'When your React app sends a "non-simple" request (such as a `POST`, `PUT`, or `DELETE` request with a `Content-Type: application/json` header or an `Authorization` Bearer token), the browser automatically performs a **Preflight Check** before sending the actual request:\n\n1. **Preflight Step**: The browser silently sends an `OPTIONS` HTTP request to the server:\n   - *"Hey server, origin http://localhost:5173 wants to send a POST request with JSON and an Authorization header. Do you permit this?"*\n2. **Server Response**:\n   - If configured correctly, the server replies with status `204 No Content` and headers:\n     ```http\n     Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:5173\n     Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS\n     Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, Authorization\n     ```\n3. **Execution**: Seeing the green light from the server, the browser proceeds to fire the real `POST` request with your payload!',hi:'Jab aap React se `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE` ya `Authorization` token bhejte hain, toh browser seedhe request nahi bhejta. Wo pehle ek **Preflight Request** bhejta hai:\n\n1. Browser chupke se ek **HTTP OPTIONS** call bhejta hai aur server se poochta hai: *"Kya origin http://localhost:5173 ko POST request bhejne ki permission hai?"*\n2. Agar server ke CORS headers allow karte hain, toh server `204 No Content` bhejta hai.\n3. Permission milte hi browser turant aapka actual POST request execute karta hai!'}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"Real-Life Analogy: The Gated Society Guard vs The Secret Underground Tunnel",hi:"Real-Life Analogy: Society Ka Security Guard vs Underground Tunnel"},body:{en:`Imagine the relationship between your React frontend and Express backend:

- **The Problem (Two Different Gated Societies)**:
  - Your React frontend is Flat 5173 in "Green Valley Apartments" (\`localhost:5173\`).
  - Your Express backend is the cloud kitchen inside "Royal Business Park" (\`localhost:5000\`).
  - You order food from the kitchen. When the delivery rider arrives at your society gate, the strict security guard (the web browser's Same-Origin Policy) blocks him: *"You have a Royal Business Park uniform! You cannot enter Green Valley without an authorized visitor gate pass!"*
- **Solution A: Express CORS Header (The Visitor Pass)**:
  The kitchen manager sends an official stamped letter to the security guard: *"Residents of Green Valley Flat 5173 are permitted to receive our food parcels."* The guard inspects the pass (\`Access-Control-Allow-Origin\`) and lets the delivery boy through!
- **Solution B: Vite Development Proxy (The Underground Tunnel)**:
  Instead of dealing with the security guard at all, the developer digs a private, underground tunnel between Flat 5173 and the kitchen. From the resident's perspective, they just walk into their own basement (\`/api/users\`), and the food appears right in their hands. As far as the security guard knows, nobody ever left the building! Zero CORS friction in development!`,hi:'Ek gated society aur restaurant ka example dekhein:\n\n- **Problem (Alag-Alag Society Gate)**:\n  React aapka ghar hai (`localhost:5173`) aur Express sadak ke us paar ka restaurant (`localhost:5000`).\n  Jab delivery boy khana lekar society gate par aata hai, toh security guard (Web Browser) use rok deta hai: *"Tum doosre compound ke ho! Bina entry pass ke andar nahi ja sakte!"*\n- **Solution A: Express CORS Middleware (Security Pass)**:\n  Restaurant manager security guard ko official letter bhejta hai: *"Flat 5173 ke residents ke liye deliveries allowed hain."* Guard letter check karta hai (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`) aur parcel andar aane deta hai.\n- **Solution B: Vite Development Proxy (Private Basement Tunnel)**:\n  Sadak par guard se ladne ke bajaye society ke basement se restaurant tak ek secret private tunnel bana di jaati hai. React ko lagta hai ki khana uske apne hi basement (`/api`) se aa raha hai, isliye browser security guard beech mein bolta hi nahi!'}},{type:"syntax",heading:{en:"Syntax & Setup: Express CORS vs Vite Development Proxy",hi:"Syntax Aur Setup: Express CORS Package Aur Vite Proxy"},body:{en:`There are two complementary ways to solve CORS in a modern MERN stack:

### Method 1: Express Backend CORS Middleware (Production & Dev)
Install \`cors\` package in \`server/\`:
\`\`\`bash
npm install cors --prefix server
\`\`\`

\`\`\`javascript
// server/src/server.js
import express from 'express';
import cors from 'cors';

const app = express();

// Configure CORS with explicit origin whitelist
const allowedOrigins = [
  'http://localhost:5173', // Vite dev
  'http://localhost:3000', // React fallback
  'https://my-production-domain.com', // Production cloud frontend
];

app.use(
  cors({
    origin: function (origin, callback) {
      // Allow requests with no origin (like mobile apps, curl, postman)
      if (!origin || allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) {
        callback(null, true);
      } else {
        callback(new Error('Blocked by CORS security policy'));
      }
    },
    credentials: true, // Allow cookies & authorization headers
    methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE', 'OPTIONS'],
    allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  })
);
\`\`\`

---

### Method 2: Vite Development Proxy (Development Workflow)
In \`client/vite.config.js\`, configure Vite to forward any request starting with \`/api\` to the backend:

\`\`\`javascript
// client/vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      '/api': {
        target: 'http://localhost:5000', // Express server port
        changeOrigin: true,
        secure: false,
      },
    },
  },
});
\`\`\`

With this proxy configured, in your React components you simply write:
\`\`\`javascript
// No localhost:5000 needed! Browser thinks request is same-origin!
const response = await fetch('/api/v1/users');
\`\`\``,hi:"CORS solve karne ke do best practices:\n\n### 1. Express Backend Par CORS Package:\n`server/` mein `npm i cors` install karein aur `app.use(cors({ origin: 'http://localhost:5173', credentials: true }))` lagayein.\n\n### 2. Vite Development Proxy:\n`client/vite.config.js` mein `server.proxy` configure karein taaki har `/api` request automatically `http://localhost:5000` par forward ho jaye. Isse React code mein sirf relative path `fetch('/api/users')` likhna padta hai."}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 1: Production-Ready Express CORS Middleware Configuration",hi:"Example 1: Production-Ready Express CORS Middleware Setup"},body:{en:`This example handles dynamic environment-based origin whitelists, preflight caching (\`maxAge\`), and credentialed cookies for secure user sessions.

\`\`\`javascript
// server/src/middleware/corsConfig.js
import cors from 'cors';

export function configureCors() {
  const isProduction = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production';

  const whiteList = isProduction
    ? [process.env.CLIENT_URL || 'https://learnhub.app']
    : ['http://localhost:5173', 'http://127.0.0.1:5173'];

  return cors({
    origin: (origin, callback) => {
      // Allow server-to-server or Postman requests (where origin is undefined)
      if (!origin || whiteList.indexOf(origin) !== -1) {
        callback(null, true);
      } else {
        callback(new Error(\`Origin \${origin} is not allowed by CORS\`));
      }
    },
    credentials: true, // Crucial for sending httpOnly auth cookies!
    methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE', 'OPTIONS'],
    allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization', 'X-Requested-With'],
    maxAge: 86400, // Cache preflight response for 24 hours (reduces OPTIONS traffic!)
  });
}

// In server.js:
// app.use(configureCors());
\`\`\``,hi:"Yeh production grade CORS configuration hai:\n- Development mein localhost allow karta hai, production mein sirf official live domain.\n- `credentials: true` cookies allow karta hai.\n- `maxAge: 86400` browser ko 24 ghante ke liye preflight OPTIONS cache karne ko bolta hai jisse har button click par faltu preflight network call na lage."}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2: Full Vite Proxy Setup with Path Rewriting",hi:"Example 2: Vite Development Proxy Aur Path Rewriting"},body:{en:`If your Express backend routes do not contain an \`/api\` prefix (e.g. \`app.get('/users')\`), you can use Vite's \`rewrite\` function to strip the prefix automatically during proxy forwarding:

\`\`\`javascript
// client/vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    open: true,
    proxy: {
      // Forward /api/users -> http://localhost:5000/users
      '/api': {
        target: 'http://localhost:5000',
        changeOrigin: true,
        rewrite: (path) => path.replace(/^\\/api/, ''),
        configure: (proxy, options) => {
          proxy.on('error', (err, req, res) => {
            console.log('Vite Proxy Error:', err);
          });
          proxy.on('proxyReq', (proxyReq, req, res) => {
            console.log(\`Proxying \${req.method} request to: \${req.url}\`);
          });
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
\`\`\``,hi:"Vite Proxy ka path rewrite feature:\nAgar backend mein route sirf `/users` hai lekin frontend par aap `/api/users` call karna chahte hain, toh `rewrite: (path) => path.replace(/^\\/api/, '')` laga kar prefix clean kar sakte hain."}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3: Handling Credentials & Cookies with CORS",hi:"Example 3: CORS Ke Saath Secure httpOnly Cookies Bhejna"},body:{en:`When sending authentication cookies (JWT stored in an \`httpOnly\` cookie) across origins, both the client AND the server must explicitly enable credentials:

\`\`\`javascript
// 1. FRONTEND: client/src/services/api.js (Axios)
import axios from 'axios';

export const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || 'http://localhost:5000/api',
  withCredentials: true, // Crucial: Tells the browser to send cookies cross-origin!
});
\`\`\`

\`\`\`javascript
// 2. BACKEND: server/server.js (Express)
import express from 'express';
import cors from 'cors';

const app = express();

app.use(
  cors({
    origin: 'http://localhost:5173', // MUST be specific origin! CANNOT be '*'!
    credentials: true,               // Crucial: Tells the browser to accept cookies!
  })
);
\`\`\`

> **CRITICAL RULE**: If \`credentials: true\` is enabled, the server **CANNOT** use \`origin: '*'\`. The browser will immediately reject the response with a fatal error! It must specify an exact, verified origin string.`,hi:"Jab login session ke liye secure cookies use hoti hain:\n1. **Frontend**: Axios mein `withCredentials: true` lagana zaroori hai.\n2. **Backend**: Express CORS mein `credentials: true` lagana zaroori hai.\n3. **Sabse Zaroori Niyam**: Cookies bhejte waqt `origin: '*'` wildcard strictly MANA hai! Wahan exact origin (`'http://localhost:5173'`) hona zaroori hai."}},{type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"Common Mistakes & How to Fix Them",hi:"Common Mistakes Aur Unke Fixes"},body:{en:`### 1. Using Wildcard Origin (*) With credentials: true
- **Mistake**: Writing \`app.use(cors({ origin: '*', credentials: true }))\`.
- **Why it breaks**: The W3C CORS specification strictly forbids credentials with wildcard origins to prevent malicious phishing websites from stealing sensitive user cookies!
- **Fix**: Specify explicit origins: \`origin: 'http://localhost:5173'\` or an array of allowed origins.

### 2. Testing for CORS Errors in Postman
- **Mistake**: Making a request in Postman, seeing a 200 OK, and concluding: *"Hey, CORS is working fine! Why is React complaining?"*
- **Why this is wrong**: **Postman is NOT a web browser!** Postman is an HTTP client with zero Same-Origin Policy enforcement. CORS is purely a browser-enforced security policy. Always test cross-origin requests in Google Chrome or Edge.

### 3. Assuming Backend 500 Errors Are CORS Errors
- **Mistake**: When Express crashes (e.g. unhandled syntax error or database connection failure), it may fail to send CORS headers, causing the browser to log a CORS error in red.
- **Fix**: Always inspect your terminal's Node.js backend logs first! Often the underlying bug is an Express 500 runtime crash, not a CORS misconfiguration.

### 4. Placing cors() Middleware After Route Declarations
- **Mistake**: Calling \`app.use('/api', routes)\` BEFORE \`app.use(cors())\`.
- **Fix**: \`app.use(cors())\` must be declared **before** any route handlers in your Express middleware stack.`,hi:`### 1. Wildcard (*) Aur credentials: true Ko Saath Mein Likhna
- **Galti**: \`cors({ origin: '*', credentials: true })\` likhna.
- **Nuksan**: Browser security rules ke mutabiq yeh error throw karta hai aur cookies delete kar deta hai.
- **Fix**: Hamesha exact origin specify karein (\`http://localhost:5173\`).

### 2. Postman Mein CORS Test Karna
- **Galti**: Postman mein check karna. Postman koi browser nahi hai, isliye wahan Same-Origin Policy hoti hi nahi! CORS hamesha browser mein test karein.

### 3. Backend Crash Ko CORS Error Samajh Lena
- **Galti**: Agar backend mein koi crash ho jata hai, toh Express headers nahi bhej pata aur browser red CORS error dikhata hai. Pehle terminal mein Node.js ke logs check karein.

### 4. cors() Ko Routes Ke Baad Likhna
- **Fix**: \`app.use(cors())\` ko hamesha Express routes se upar likhein.`}},{type:"tip",heading:{en:"Best Practices: Full-Stack CORS Architecture",hi:"Best Practices: Full-Stack CORS Architecture"},body:{en:"1. **Use Vite Proxy for Local Development**: Configuring Vite proxy solves CORS on developer machines completely and allows using clean relative paths (`/api/users`).\n2. **Set Preflight maxAge**: Add `maxAge: 86400` in Express CORS options. This instructs browsers to cache OPTIONS preflight responses for 24 hours, eliminating 50% of your network roundtrips!\n3. **Use Environment Variables for Allowed Origins**: Never hardcode localhost or staging URLs in your production backend code. Keep allowed origins in `process.env.CLIENT_ORIGIN`.\n4. **Log Blocked Origins in Development**: In your CORS origin callback, log any blocked origins to the terminal so you can instantly diagnose typos like missing trailing slashes or `http` vs `https`.",hi:"1. **Local Dev Ke Liye Vite Proxy**: Development mein Vite proxy use karein taaki relative paths (`/api/users`) se clean coding ho sake.\n2. **Preflight Caching**: `maxAge: 86400` lagayein taaki OPTIONS requests baar-baar na bhejni padein.\n3. **Environment Variables**: Allowed domains ko hamesha `process.env.CLIENT_ORIGIN` mein rakhein.\n4. **Blocked Origins Debugging**: Terminal mein origin print karein agar koi request reject ho rahi ho taaki spelling mistake pakad sakein."}},{type:"interview",heading:{en:"Top Interview Questions & Answers",hi:"Interview Ke Zaroori Sawal Aur Jawab"},body:{en:'### Q1: What is the Same-Origin Policy, and what entity enforces it?\n**Answer**: The Same-Origin Policy (SOP) is a critical security standard implemented and enforced strictly by **web browsers**. It prevents malicious scripts loaded on one origin (e.g. `evil-phishing.com`) from reading sensitive data or executing unauthorized API calls against another origin (e.g. `mybank.com`). It is NOT enforced by servers or non-browser HTTP clients like Postman.\n\n### Q2: What defines a "Preflight" request and when does a browser trigger one?\n**Answer**: A preflight request is an automated HTTP `OPTIONS` request sent by the browser before the actual request. The browser triggers a preflight request if the request is "non-simple", such as:\n1. Using HTTP methods other than `GET`, `HEAD`, or `POST`.\n2. Setting headers other than basic standard headers (e.g. setting `Authorization: Bearer <token>`).\n3. Using a `Content-Type` other than `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`, `multipart/form-data`, or `text/plain` (e.g. sending `application/json`).\n\n### Q3: Why is Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * forbidden when using cookies or credentials?\n**Answer**: If a server responded with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` and allowed credentials, any malicious third-party website on the internet could make credentialed background requests to your banking API using the user\'s active session cookies and read the response. The CORS specification strictly forbids this combination.\n\n### Q4: How does a Vite development proxy eliminate CORS errors during local development?\n**Answer**: In the browser, requests are sent to the same origin (`http://localhost:5173/api/...`). Since the protocol, host, and port match the React page\'s origin, the browser\'s Same-Origin Policy does not trigger CORS checks. The Vite dev server (acting as a local Node reverse proxy) then forwards the request over local TCP to `http://localhost:5000`. Because server-to-server communication is not subject to browser SOP, no CORS headers are required.',hi:"### Q1: Same-Origin Policy kya hai aur ise kaun enforce karta hai?\n**Jawab**: Same-Origin Policy browser ke dwara enforce kiya gaya security rule hai jo ek website ko doosri website ka data churaney se rokta hai. Yeh rule sirf web browsers mein lagu hota hai, servers ya Postman par nahi.\n\n### Q2: Preflight request kab trigger hoti hai?\n**Jawab**: Jab request non-simple ho: jaise `POST` ya `PUT` mein `application/json` bhejna ya `Authorization` header attach karna. Browser pehle `OPTIONS` call bhejkar server se permission leta hai.\n\n### Q3: Wildcard (*) ke saath cookies bhejna kyun mana hai?\n**Jawab**: Agar wildcard par cookies allow kar di jayein, toh koi bhi hacker website aapke bank account par aapki cookies ke saath request bhejkar aapka balance read kar legi. Security ke liye browser ise block karta hai.\n\n### Q4: Vite Proxy se CORS kaise gayab ho jata hai?\n**Jawab**: Browser request apne hi origin (`localhost:5173`) par bhejta hai, isliye Same-Origin Policy trigger hi nahi hoti. Vite server background mein use backend (`localhost:5000`) par forward kar deta hai."}},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"Quick Summary: CORS & Proxy Cheatsheet",hi:"Quick Summary: CORS & Proxy Cheatsheet"},body:{en:"- **Same-Origin Policy**: Enforced by browsers across Protocol, Domain, and Port.\n- **CORS Headers**: Server-side headers granting cross-origin read permissions to browsers.\n- **Preflight (OPTIONS)**: Automatic check sent before JSON `POST`/`PUT`/`DELETE` or `Authorization` headers.\n- **Vite Proxy**: `server.proxy` in `vite.config.js` routes `/api` calls seamlessly during development.\n- **Credentials Rule**: `credentials: true` requires an explicit origin; never use wildcard `*`.\n- **Preflight Caching**: Set `maxAge: 86400` in Express CORS to reduce redundant `OPTIONS` traffic.",hi:"- **Same-Origin Policy**: Browser ka security guard jo alag port ko block karta hai.\n- **CORS Headers**: Express backend se browser ko permission dene wale headers.\n- **Preflight Check**: `OPTIONS` request jo JSON ya token bhejte waqt pehle aati hai.\n- **Vite Proxy**: Local development mein bina CORS ke API connect karne ka best tareeqa.\n- **Credentials Niyam**: Cookies bhejte waqt hamesha specific domain likhein, `*` nahi.\n- **Preflight Cache**: `maxAge` se OPTIONS requests ko 24 ghante ke liye cache karein."}}],quiz:[{question:{en:"Why does sending an API request to http://localhost:5000 from http://localhost:5173 trigger a CORS error?",hi:"http://localhost:5173 se http://localhost:5000 par API request bhejne par CORS error kyun aata hai?"},options:[{en:"Because localhost is banned by the internet consortium",hi:"Kyunki localhost internet par banned hai"},{en:"Because the ports differ (5173 vs 5000), which violates the browser's Same-Origin Policy unless permitted by CORS headers",hi:"Kyunki dono ke ports alag hain (5173 vs 5000), jo Same-Origin Policy ke tahat alag origin maana jata hai jab tak server CORS headers na de"},{en:"Because Node.js does not support HTTP requests",hi:"Kyunki Node.js HTTP requests support nahi karta"},{en:"Because JavaScript cannot parse JSON numbers",hi:"Kyunki JavaScript JSON numbers parse nahi kar sakta"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"An origin consists of protocol + domain + port. Even on localhost, port 5173 and port 5000 are distinct origins, triggering browser CORS checks.",hi:"Origin mein protocol, domain aur port teeno aate hain. Port alag hone ki wajah se browser ise cross-origin request manta hai."}},{question:{en:"Which HTTP method does the browser automatically send as a CORS preflight request?",hi:"Browser CORS preflight request ke roop mein kaunsa HTTP method automatically bhejta hai?"},options:[{en:"HEAD",hi:"HEAD"},{en:"OPTIONS",hi:"OPTIONS"},{en:"CHECK",hi:"CHECK"},{en:"TRACE",hi:"TRACE"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"The browser sends an HTTP OPTIONS request before executing non-simple requests to ask the server for permission.",hi:"Browser actual request se pehle HTTP OPTIONS method ke zariye server se permission leta hai."}},{question:{en:"Why is Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * strictly forbidden when credentials (cookies/auth headers) are enabled?",hi:"Credentials (cookies/auth headers) enabled hone par Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * strictly mana kyun hai?"},options:[{en:"It would allow any malicious website to steal authenticated session cookies and user data",hi:"Isse koi bhi hacker website authenticated session cookies aur user data chura sakti hai"},{en:"Asterisks are not allowed in HTTP header specifications",hi:"HTTP headers mein asterisk allowed nahi hote"},{en:"It makes the database query take 10 times longer",hi:"Isse database query bohot slow ho jaati hai"},{en:"It disables HTTPS encryption",hi:"Yeh HTTPS encryption disable kar deta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Allowing wildcards with credentials would expose users to cross-site request hijacking and data exfiltration. The CORS specification prohibits wildcards when credentials: true.",hi:"Security ke liye wildcard ke saath cookies allow nahi hoti taaki malicious websites user ke sensitive authenticated data ko access na kar sakein."}},{question:{en:"How does configuring a development proxy in vite.config.js bypass CORS errors during local development?",hi:"vite.config.js mein development proxy configure karne se local development mein CORS error kaise solve hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It disables JavaScript security in Google Chrome",hi:"Yeh Chrome mein JavaScript security disable kar deta hai"},{en:"The browser sends requests to its own origin (/api), and the Vite dev server forwards them to Express via local TCP, avoiding browser cross-origin checks",hi:"Browser apne hi origin par request bhejta hai (/api), aur Vite dev server background mein Express ko forward kar deta hai, jisse browser CORS trigger hi nahi hota"},{en:"It compresses all image files",hi:"Yeh saari image files compress kar deta hai"},{en:"It converts Express into a React component",hi:"Yeh Express ko React component mein convert kar deta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"A dev proxy makes requests appear same-origin to the browser. The server-to-server proxy forwarding has no browser Same-Origin Policy restrictions.",hi:"Vite proxy se browser ko lagta hai ki request same origin par ho rahi hai, aur server-to-server communication par browser SOP lagu nahi hoti."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling cors configuration & vite proxy setup with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup directly resolve?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"Modular design CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup in production?",hi:"Production mein CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in CORS Configuration & Vite Proxy Setup?",hi:"CORS Problem & Vite Proxy Setup mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}}]};export{e as default};
